## Adapt appearance across legacy and modern SDKs

When targeting legacy operating systems like iOS 16 alongside modern releases, avoid relying entirely on behaviors exclusive to newer design paradigms. Use `UINavigationBarAppearance` to explicitly manage bar backgrounds on older targets while letting the system automatically apply scroll edge effects and design styling on devices running modern SDKs.

- TN3106: Customizing the appearance of UINavigationBar

1. Configure standard and scroll-edge appearances for navigation bars to maintain visual consistency on iOS 16.
2. Remove hardcoded opaque background tints on modern target blocks so the system can properly render adaptive materials where available.
3. Test the search workflow thoroughly on physical or simulated iPhone X hardware running iOS 16 to verify keyboard layouts and touch targets.

- TN3106: Customizing the appearance of UINavigationBar

